# Pink Pepper Lavender — Masculine Aromatic-Fougère

## 30 mL EdP, ~20% concentrate (6,000 µL concentrate)

**Status:** DESIGN FOCUS / CURRENT-INVENTORY BUILD / NOT COMPOUNDED / NOT TESTED / RELEASE HOLD  
**Concept:** Pink pepper (Schinus molle) as the lead voice in a masculine lavender structure. The rosy-spicy character of pink pepper dominates the opening, supported by spike lavender's camphoraceous lift, and dries down to a clean woody-amber base.

**Family:** Aromatic-fougère  
**Concentration:** EdP (~20%)  
**Target:** 30 mL bottle  

## TARGET / IDEAL versus CURRENT-INVENTORY BUILD

| Layer | TARGET / IDEAL | CURRENT-INVENTORY translation |
|---|---|---|
| Pink pepper identity | Schinus molle signature as a fresh rosy-spicy leading note | kept as neat `Pink Pepper EO (Schinus molle)` from user-confirmed current stock |
| Pink pepper CO₂ material | Any CO₂/steam-partition requirement rows are separate lineage controls | **not used** in this build; CO₂ references remain separate and non-equivalent |
| Lavender identity | aromatic-camphoraceous lavender with masculine edge | Spike Lavender EO at stock scale |
| Concentrate target | 6,000 µL exactly, 20% total for 30 mL | 6,000 µL used with no unresolved top-up stock |

